 match, however, for the French crew of " [:a {:href "/athletes/62731"} "Jean-Yves le Déroff"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/62317"} "Nicolas Hénard"] " who won three of the first five races and finished second in the other two, and did not even start the final race, their gold medal assured. Timms and Sellars comfortably won the silver medal over Brazil’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/62179"} "Lars Grael"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/62049"} "Clinio Freitas"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "With a different partner, Lars Grael would return in 1996 and win another bronze in this class. He was the brother of " [:a {:href "/athletes/62180"} "Torben Grael"] ", bronze medalist in the Star class in Busan, who would eventually win five Olympic sailing medals. The Danish boat in 15th class was skippered by " [:a {:href "/athletes/61927"} "Paul Elvstrøm"] ", competing in his eighth Olympics, and looking for his fifth gold medal, after winning the one-person dinghy class at four consecutive Olympics, 1948-60. This was the end of his remarkable Olympic career."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Net Points"] [:th {} "Total Points"] [:th {} "Race #1"] [:th {} "Race #2"] [:th {} "Race #3"] [:th {} "Race #4"] [:th {} "Race #5"] [:th {} "Race #6"] [:th {} "Race #7"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "France"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "16.0"] [:td {} "46.0"] [:td {} ".0 (1)"] [:td {} "3.0 (2)"] [:td {} "3.0 (2)"] [:td {} ".0 (1)"] [:td {} ".0 (1)"] [:td {} "10.0 (5)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "17"} [:a {:href "/athletes/62731"} "Jean-Yves Le Déroff"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/62317"} "Nicolas Héna